  "id": "t-distribution",
  "term": "t distribution",
  "definition": "The t distribution is a probability distribution for a value from a normal distribution after it is divided by an estimated standard deviation. In research, it is commonly used for statistics such as a mean or the difference between means when the standard error is estimated, and it has a more peaked shape with heavier tails than a normal distribution.",
